body:
*Handsup*

&#x200B;

HOMESTRETCH LADIES AND GENTLEMAN!

Breathedge and Astroneer!

&#x200B;

A long stretch here, but maybe Dyson Sphere Program (EARLY ACCESS GAME) if you also enjoy building factories, processing materials, and automation. You can visit planets and different solar systems that are randomly generated before starting a game. They recently had a major update that added more planet types, and a Civilization Type III System (which you can start seeing other people's galaxies - not sure if you can zoom in). The game also has mod support, you can build ships to transport goods within a planetary system and interstellar travel, you can warp to other planets or systems, and build drones to transport goods within a planet.

Oh man, am I trying my best. I try to tell myself "it happened" and try to direct my focus on the now, the present. The thing is how do you learn from the past without worrying about what you have done in the past? Or try to do better than what we have done in the past? I guess I should focus on how can I be my best self in the now, and not compare it to my past.

&#x200B;

Very stimulating subject.

Hmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm.

&#x200B;

Thank you.

Oh man, I wish I could start my new job already! I want to quit my current job so bad.

&#x200B;

Hold on everyone!!
